            Embed it in Rust. <span class="candy-text">Call Rust like a module.</span>
          </h2>
          <p>
            The <code>skathi</code> crate runs the whole engine inside your executable, on a thread of its own, and
            <code>main</code> stays yours. Mark an <code>impl</code> block <code>#[skathi::module]</code> and the app imports
            its methods from <code>native:notes</code>. Values cross straight between Rust and the engine with no JSON
            in between, and a <code>&amp;[u8]</code> reads the app's bytes where they are.
          </p>
          <p>
            A <code>pub fn</code> returns its value inside the call, a <code>#[task]</code> runs on a worker and returns a
            promise, and events reach <code>on</code> from any thread. <code>sk types --exe</code> asks your exe for its modules
            and writes the app's <code>.d.ts</code>, so a renamed field fails the type check, not a user.
          </p>
